IF @setup_complete == TRUE
    PRINT Report the verified private tool versions, authentication states, and @host.bin.
    RETURN "Setup already complete."

IF @github.ready == FALSE
    DO Select one GitHub CLI release metadata URL from @gh_releases_api. Append
        /latest when @requested_gh_version is NULL. Otherwise normalize the
        requested version to one v-prefixed tag, URL-encode it, and append
        /tags/<tag>. Return the exact URL. AS gh_release_api

    DO Install or upgrade GitHub CLI only at @host.gh. Read official release
        metadata from @gh_release_api. Select the exact @host.os and @host.arch
        archive and checksum, download into a unique private temporary directory,
        verify the exact SHA-256 before extraction, and require the requested tag
        when one was supplied.
        Create @host.bin and missing parents only when required; track newly
        created paths and remove any that remain empty before failing. Install
        the executable with required permissions, verify its version, and remove
        only the temporary directory before completing or failing. Preserve a
        working existing tool until the replacement is verified. Return an object
        with path, version, ready, and authenticated. AS github

RUN @host.gh --version AS gh_version

DO Verify @gh_version.stdout matches @github.version and @github.ready is TRUE.

IF @github.authenticated == FALSE
    PRINT "Complete GitHub browser approval when the CLI displays its login URL or device code."

    DO Run @host.gh auth login --hostname github.com --web as one interactive
        process and wait for it to finish. Keep gh-managed credentials and never
        request or expose a token. Then run only the matching auth-status check.
        Return @github updated with authenticated TRUE only after success. AS github

IF @github.authenticated != TRUE
    RETURN "Setup stopped because GitHub authentication is incomplete."

IF @atlassian.ready == FALSE
    DO Install or upgrade Atlassian CLI only at @host.acli. Inspect
        @acli_source once, select the official supported binary for @host.os and
        @host.arch, honor @requested_acli_version, and use a unique private
        temporary directory. Verify the vendor's exact SHA-256 when published;
        otherwise record that no checksum was available. Create @host.bin and
        missing parents only when required; track newly created paths and remove
        any that remain empty before failing. Install with required permissions,
        verify the version, and remove only that temporary directory before
        completing or failing. Preserve a working existing tool until the
        replacement is verified. Return an object with path, version, ready,
        authenticated, and checksum_status. AS atlassian

RUN @host.acli --version AS acli_version

DO Verify @acli_version.stdout matches @atlassian.version and @atlassian.ready is TRUE.

IF @atlassian.authenticated == FALSE
    PRINT "Complete Jira browser approval when the CLI displays its login URL."

    DO Run @host.acli jira auth login --web as one interactive process and wait
        for it to finish. Keep acli-managed credentials and never request or
        expose a token. Then run only the matching auth-status check. Return
        @atlassian updated with authenticated TRUE only after success. AS atlassian

IF @atlassian.authenticated != TRUE
    RETURN "Setup stopped because Jira authentication is incomplete."

IF @inux.ready == FALSE
    DO Install ix @host.tag from @repository only at @host.ix. Use the verified
        private @host.gh executable to download the exact host asset and
        checksums.txt into a unique private temporary directory. Select
        ix-darwin-amd64, ix-darwin-arm64, ix-linux-amd64,
        ix-linux-arm64, or ix-windows-amd64.exe as appropriate. Verify the exact
        SHA-256 before installation. Create @host.bin and missing parents only
        when required; track newly created paths and remove any that remain
        empty before failing. Preserve a working existing ix until the
        replacement is verified, set required permissions, confirm
        @host.expected_version, run --help once, and remove only that temporary
        directory before completing or failing. Return an object with path,
        version, and ready. AS inux

RUN @host.ix --version AS ix_version

DO Verify @ix_version.stdout contains exactly @host.expected_version and @inux.ready is TRUE.

RUN @host.ix --help AS ix_help

DO Recompute setup completion from @github, @atlassian, and @inux. Return TRUE
    only when all versions and both authentication checks are verified. AS setup_complete

IF @setup_complete != TRUE
    RETURN "Setup stopped because one or more required checks failed."

PRINT Report @github, @atlassian, @inux, and @host.bin in a compact table. Include checksum limitations and no tokens.
